<title>LITHUANIA: BOURSE CAPITALISATION ROSE LAST WEEK.</title>
<headline>BOURSE CAPITALISATION ROSE LAST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the</p>
<p>Lithuanian bourse rose to 5.63 billion litas during last week</p>
<p>versus 5.47 billion litas a week earlier, the stock exchange</p>
<p>said on Monday.</p>
<p>The statistics of the Vilnius bourse:</p>
<p>					   March 12-14     March 3-8</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		   7,246	   17,069</p>
<p>    Executed orders		    1,366	   1,770</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    central market (CM)		1,248	   1,456</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL	6,896,750     10,283,050</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    bloc trades (BT)		   59		99</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	    6,366,840     10,191,760</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week	24,361,656    48,610,260</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week	3,427,439     5,088,422</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	    6,775,650     6,355,460</p>
<p>    in BT per week in litas	  6,366,840     9,173,490</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T bills	    4		 6</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T bills in LTL per week	  121,000	 4,945,850</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
